 "A LangChain <0>agent</0> is the agent loop from <1>the agent loop</1> packaged up: model call → tool calls → run tools → append results → repeat until no more tool calls.": "",
 "In LangChain ≥ {#} agents are built on <0>LangGraph</0> (a graph runtime with state and checkpoints); <1/> is the high-level entry point.": "",
 "Trade-off: less boilerplate and built-in persistence/streaming vs. less visibility and another dependency.": "",
 "For custom control flow (branches, approvals, multi-agent), use LangGraph directly: <0>LangGraph section</0>.": "",
